se ranking is central; [(Chaput et al., 2016-10)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/fe7697844facb2a5106131b4d876513a2d8afba3) evaluated enrichment and BEDROC and found target-specific ranking differences that classification metrics may miss. The weakest contradiction is that the high-quality benchmark claim is weakened by under-specified curation and split details: manual curation of 4,100 actives and 24,000 inactives is feasible only if normalization, duplicate/contradiction removal, filter choices, and the relationship between the 24,000 inactives and the five balanced training sets are documented, as emphasized by [(Galushka et al., 2021-06)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/175350d719829390942b516184ae5c229efabae2) and [(Chávez-Hernández et al., 2023-06)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/d9d24516c346d5287f4826245bd0c688f4533822).",
